---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Recruitment & Staffing
description: Full-cycle staffing for employers — sourcing, screening, and delivering vetted candidates across contract, temp, and permanent roles.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
  - /assets/js/candidate-route.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   RECRUITMENT & STAFFING — creative redesign
   (see claude_helper/RECRUITMENT-STAFFING-PAGE.md).

   The employer-side hiring experience. Same IA as before:
     Hero → Transition → Included → Sectors → Terms → Process → FAQ → CTA
   What changed is composition and storytelling. The recurring device is THE
   HIRING ROUTE (partials/candidate-route.njk, shared with Job Placement):
   BRIEF → SOURCE → SCREEN → INTERVIEW → ONBOARD. Drawn incomplete in the hero;
   candidate-route.js advances it and the process trace as the reader scrolls.

   Discipline unchanged: stats, the employer wall and employer quotes stay gated
   until real, consented content exists. See the TODOs.
   ================================================================ #}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "Recruitment & Staffing" }] %}
{% set routeNodes = [
  { label: "Brief" }, { label: "Source" }, { label: "Screen" },
  { label: "Interview" }, { label: "Onboard" }
] %}

{# ---------- 1. Hero — 7/5 asymmetric editorial split ----------
   The "15 min" marker reads as a starting point, not a badge. The hiring route
   starts here, deliberately incomplete. ---------- #}
<section data-route-step="1" class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-container pb-14 pt-8 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-12">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:pr-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Contingency — you pay on placement</p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
          Hire faster,<br>hire right.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-copy mt-6 max-w-xl">
          Vetted candidates for contract, temp, or full-time roles — delivered
          faster than sifting through a job board yourself.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=employer' | url }}" class="btn-primary">
            {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }} Tell us your hiring need
          </a>
          <a href="{{ '/services/talent-acquisition/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">
            Compare with search {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
          </a>
        </div>

        {# The recurring device, drawn at its first node. #}
        {% set routeActive = 1 %}
        {% set routeProgress = true %}
        <div class="mt-12 max-w-lg">
          {% include "partials/candidate-route.njk" %}
        </div>

        {# TODO — confirm every figure with the client before launch (stats.json). #}
        <dl class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-x-12 gap-y-5 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
          {% for stat in stats.list.slice(0, 3) %}
          <div>
            <dd class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl"
                data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
            <dt class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        {% set coverImage = images.services["recruitment-staffing"].cover %}
        <figure class="jp-frame">
          <span class="jp-frame-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div class="jp-frame-media jp-reveal">
            <img src="{{ coverImage.url }}"
                 alt="{{ coverImage.alt }}"
                 width="1400" height="1750" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
                 class="aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover">
          </div>
          <figcaption class="jp-frame-caption">Requirement intake</figcaption>

          {# Frost — it floats over the photograph (THEME.md §3). #}
          <div class="glass-frost jp-fee">
            <p class="meta">To start</p>
            <p class="font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">15 min</p>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# TODO — Employer wall gated. placed-at.njk hotlinks logo.clearbit.com for named
   companies — a client list we can't substantiate. When real placements exist,
   render a HIRING LEDGER (role filled / industry, on hairlines) before any logos.
{% set placedAtTitle = "Hired through us" %}
{% set placedAtLead = "Teams that filled a role this way." %}
{% include "partials/placed-at.njk" %}
#}

{# ---------- 2. The transition — a role shouldn't sit still ----------
   A visual bridge from the problem to the recruitment system. Deliberately short;
   the brief card on the right is a decorative document, not a claim. ---------- #}
<section class="border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-14 sm:py-20">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-center lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <p class="assertion text-2xl sm:text-3xl">A role shouldn't sit still.</p>
        <p class="body-copy mt-4 max-w-xl">
          When a position needs the right person, the work starts before the first
          resume reaches your inbox.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="jp-brief" aria-hidden="true">
          <p class="meta">Open role</p>
          <dl class="mt-3 divide-y divide-ink/10 border-y border-ink/10">
            <div class="jp-brief-row"><dt>Team</dt><dd>Product</dd></div>
            <div class="jp-brief-row"><dt>Type</dt><dd>Permanent</dd></div>
            <div class="jp-brief-row"><dt>Priority</dt><dd>High</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="jp-brief-status"><span class="jp-brief-dot"></span> Sourcing</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 3. What's included — vertical editorial index ----------
   Sticky heading on lg; the four capabilities scroll past and the reader's
   current one takes the route node. ---------- #}
<section id="included" data-route-step="2" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% set included = [
    { icon: "target", t: "Candidate sourcing", d: "Active and passive candidate networks built specifically for your role, not a job-board repost." },
    { icon: "shield", t: "Screening & vetting", d: "Skills, references, and fit assessed before a candidate ever reaches your inbox." },
    { icon: "briefcase", t: "Staffing models", d: "Contract, temp-to-hire, or permanent — whichever structure fits the role." },
    { icon: "users", t: "Industry specializations", d: "Dedicated sourcing pipelines in technology, finance, healthcare, and more." }
  ] %}

  <div class="grid gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-[17rem_1fr] lg:gap-x-16">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <h2 class="section-title">Four things every engagement gets.</h2>
      <p class="lead-copy mt-4">
        Built for how you actually hire, whatever the role structure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="jp-index" data-jp-index>
      {% for item in included %}
      <li class="jp-index-row" data-jp-item>
        <div class="jp-index-head">
          <span class="jp-index-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
          <span class="jp-index-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="jp-index-icon">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card-title mt-3">{{ item.t }}</h3>
        <p class="body-copy mt-1.5">{{ item.d }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 4. Where we place — the hiring landscape ----------
   A numbered sector index, not a card grid. Employers scan for their own sector
   first, so this sits high. Hovering a sector lights its node. ---------- #}
<section id="sectors" data-route-step="3" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="section-title">Where we place.</h2>
      <p class="lead-copy mt-4">Employers scan for their own sector first. Here's ours.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="jp-sectors">
      {% for industry in industries.list %}
      <li class="jp-sector">
        <div class="jp-sector-head">
          <span class="jp-sector-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
          <span class="jp-sector-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="jp-sector-icon">{{ icon(industry.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="jp-sector-name">{{ industry.name }}</p>
        <p class="jp-sector-roles">{{ industry.roles }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 5. How engagements work — the hiring contract ----------
   Structure, not rates. The terms prose runs wide-left; the "at a glance" panel
   is the quick-reference beside it. ---------- #}
<section id="terms" data-route-step="4" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">How engagements work.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:items-start lg:gap-12">
    <dl class="jp-terms lg:col-span-3">
      {% set terms = [
        { t: "Permanent placements", d: "Contingency-based. You pay when someone starts, not before." },
        { t: "Contract & temp", d: "A flat markup on hourly billing, quoted upfront." },
        { t: "No retainer", d: "Nothing to begin, and no minimum for a one-off role." },
        { t: "Ongoing partnerships", d: "Move to a dedicated account structure once volume picks up." }
      ] %}
      {% for term in terms %}
      <div class="jp-term">
        <dt class="jp-term-t">{{ term.t }}</dt>
        <dd class="jp-term-d">{{ term.d }}</dd>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </dl>

    <div class="jp-glance lg:col-span-2">
      <p class="meta">Terms at a glance</p>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
          <dt class="mt-0.5 meta">Permanent</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm font-medium leading-snug text-ink">Contingency — you pay on placement</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
          <dt class="mt-0.5 meta">Contract</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm font-medium leading-snug text-ink">Flat hourly markup, no retainer</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
          <dt class="mt-0.5 meta">To start</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm font-medium leading-snug text-ink">A role brief and 15 minutes</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=employer' | url }}" class="mt-5 link-arrow">
        Tell us your hiring need {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="jp-note mt-10 max-w-2xl">
    Rates depend on role and seniority — we'll quote before any work begins.
  </p>
</section>

{# ---------- 6. The process — a horizontal recruitment trace ----------
   Ordinal; the node the reader is level with is the current step, earlier nodes
   read as completed. Vertical trace on mobile. ---------- #}
<section id="procedure" data-route-step="5" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    {% set steps = [
      { label: "Requirement analysis", description: "We start with the role, the team, and what \"right\" actually looks like." },
      { label: "Sourcing", description: "Active outreach across our network, not a passive posting." },
      { label: "Screening", description: "Skills and reference checks before you see a single resume." },
      { label: "Client interviews", description: "A shortlist you can actually choose from." },
      { label: "Onboarding", description: "Support through the offer and the first day." }
    ] %}
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Step by step</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mt-2">From requirement to onboarding.</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="jp-journey mt-14" data-jp-journey>
      {% for step in steps %}
      <li class="jp-journey-step{% if loop.first %} is-current{% endif %}" data-jp-node>
        <span class="jp-journey-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
        <span class="jp-journey-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p class="jp-journey-label">{{ step.label }}</p>
        <p class="jp-journey-desc">{{ step.description }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

